# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies. Three copies of node_modules, ~35 MB, all restorable
# with npm install.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Android build output. android-app/android/ is 33 MB of Gradle and
# Capacitor scaffolding that `npx cap sync` regenerates, and www/ is a
# COPY of client/ that the Capacitor build makes — committing it would
# mean every client change showed up twice in the diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
android-app/android/
android-app/www/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore
.gradle/
build/
local.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated screenshots, 14 MB and rising.
#
# These are worth taking seriously — photographs have caught four bugs
# on this project that no test could, because every check asks whether
# you can walk somewhere and none of them asks whether the building
# looks like the building. But they are regenerated by
# tools/checks/_templeshot.mjs on demand, and they change on every
# render tweak, which would bloat the history fast.
#
# Ignored for now. If you want the visual history, the right fix is a
# few chosen reference shots committed deliberately, not all of them
# committed automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
docs/shots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored, deliberately, though both are large:
#
#   client/vendor/        3.1 MB — vendored Three.js. This project has
#                         NO BUILD STEP; the browser imports these
#                         files directly through the import map. They
#                         are source, not a dependency.
#
#   tools/osm-import/raw/ 3.5 MB — cached Overpass responses. These
#                         make the OpenStreetMap import reproducible
#                         without re-querying, and docs/DATA-SOURCES.md
#                         relies on them for the ODbL provenance
#                         record. Losing them would mean losing the
#                         evidence that the world data is legitimately
#                         sourced.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

